# desktop.pkgs — NCZ-OS 26.7 "Maximilian" Singularity Desktop offline closure.
#
# Singularity Desktop (labwc/wlroots, GTK4/Vala, GLES on CIX libmali) replaces
# XFCE/X11. This seed is the runtime closure build-desktop-mirror.sh resolves +
# bundles into the ISO pool so post-install/20-desktop.sh installs the desktop
# fully OFFLINE from file:///cdrom. NO xubuntu-core, NO xfce4-*, NO Xorg display
# server. Xwayland IS kept (X-app compat under Wayland).
#
# The Singularity shell binaries ship in /opt/singularity (singularity-opt.tgz);
# the packages here are the SYSTEM libs they link against + the session infra.
#
# ncz-singularity-desktop (real Debian package, build/build-singularity-deb.sh
# wraps singularity-opt.tgz) MUST be in this seed — post-install/20-desktop.sh
# does `apt-get install ncz-singularity-desktop`, not a raw tarball extract
# (that was an earlier design; the code moved to a real package, this seed
# entry was never added to match — found + fixed 2026-07-27 running the
# offline-mirror build for real for what looks like the first time: without
# it, 20-desktop.sh hard-fails with "ncz-singularity-desktop not installable"
# on any build that doesn't happen to have live network access to Buildkite).

# --- greeter (SHIP: greetd + NATIVE singularity-greeter) --------------------
# greetd is the display manager; the greeter is the native singularity-greeter
# (wlr-layer-shell + Cairo/loginui), shipped in the /opt/singularity payload — no
# distro greeter package. glycin-loaders = image loaders the Singularity shell
# uses. NO lightdm (X11), NO regreet — Singularity is Wayland/Mali native.
greetd
glycin-loaders
ncz-singularity-desktop

# --- Singularity runtime libraries (what /opt/singularity binaries link) ----
libgtk-4-1
libadwaita-1-0
libgtk4-layer-shell0
libgee-0.8-2
libpeas-2-0
libjson-glib-1.0-0
libsoup-3.0-0
libvte-2.91-gtk4-0
libgtksourceview-5-0
libwebkitgtk-6.0-4
libgraphene-1.0-0
# The payload links these directly; keep them explicit because the current
# package artifact predates correct shlib dependency generation.
libtinysparql-3.0-0
libupower-glib3
libdbusmenu-glib4
libsodium26
upower
gsettings-desktop-schemas
libglib2.0-bin

# --- Wayland session infra --------------------------------------------------
foot
xsettingsd
seatd
libseat1
libliftoff0
libxcb-composite0
libxcb-ewmh2
# labwc links libxcb-errors for readable X11 protocol errors under Xwayland.
libxcb-errors0
swaybg
grim
slurp
fuzzel
xwayland
polkitd
xdg-desktop-portal

# --- native Wayland screensaver / idle-lock (57-screensaver) ----------------
# swayidle = wlroots ext-idle-notify idle timer; swaylock = fallback blank lock
# (the native Singularity lockscreen is primary); wlopm = wlr-output-power DPMS.
# These REPLACE X11 xscreensaver (NOT in this closure — wrong stack for Mali/WL).
swayidle
swaylock
wlopm
# "Screensaver & Lock" config app (ncz-screensaver-settings) is Python GTK4 +
# libadwaita — needs the GObject-introspection bindings + typelibs at runtime
# (the Vala Singularity apps link the libs directly and don't pull these).
python3-gi
gir1.2-gtk-4.0
gir1.2-adw-1
gir1.2-glib-2.0

# --- GPU / GL tooling (Mali GLES; Vulkan tools for diagnostics) -------------
mesa-utils
vulkan-tools
libglu1-mesa
clinfo
glmark2-es2-wayland
glmark2-wayland

# --- audio (PipeWire) -------------------------------------------------------
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber
pavucontrol

# --- removable media + network + bluetooth ---------------------------------
# NETWORK: NCZ-OS 26.7 ships the NATIVE Singularity network daemon `sinty-nm`
# (Go, static, /usr/bin/sinty-nmd) which OWNS org.freedesktop.NetworkManager on
# the system bus (a full NM replacement, wire-compatible with libnm/nmcli). So
# NetworkManager + network-manager-gnome are NOT shipped (20-desktop purges/masks
# NM). iwd = the WiFi backend sinty-nm drives; wireguard-tools = its VPN backend.
gvfs
gvfs-backends
udisks2
gnome-disk-utility
iwd
wireguard-tools
bluez
blueman

# --- fonts ------------------------------------------------------------------
fonts-noto-core
fonts-noto-cjk
fonts-noto-color-emoji
fonts-liberation

# --- browser + media -------------------------------------------------------
# Vivaldi installs from the staged upstream .deb in 52-vivaldi.sh and remains
# the default browser. Real, official Google Chrome for arm64 Linux (public
# since Q2 2026, via Google's own signed apt repo) is the second browser —
# build-desktop-mirror folds it into the offline desktop pool, pinned +
# SHA256-verified against Google's published Packages index; no live apt
# source on the shipped image, no snapd. ungoogled-chromium/XtraDeb (an
# earlier stop-gap from before real Chrome existed for arm64) is dropped —
# real Chrome supersedes it outright.
google-chrome-stable
mpv

# --- archives + PDF + image (GTK, DE-agnostic) -----------------------------
xarchiver
7zip
unrar-free
evince

# --- offline-apt tools (usable from the desktop with no network) -----------
synaptic
gdebi
gdebi-core
# software-properties-gtk is Ubuntu's PPA GUI.  NCZ uses its signed NCZ
# repository plus Debian sources, so it has no role on the Debian base.

# --- keyring / disk-usage ---------------------------------------------------
# KEYRING: the NATIVE `singularity-keyring` (in /opt/singularity, D-Bus-activated
# org.freedesktop.secrets) is THE Secret Service — gnome-keyring is NOT shipped
# (20-desktop purges it; it would otherwise grab the secrets name first). seahorse
# is dropped with it (seahorse depends on gnome-keyring; Singularity has its own
# secret UI).
baobab

# --- image editing ----------------------------------------------------------
gimp

# --- runtime deps other hooks rely on (branding/avatars, agents) -----------
# NO plymouth — the boot splash is the native KMS singularity-boot-splash
# (/opt/singularity payload), 60-boot-splash purges plymouth outright.
librsvg2-bin
imagemagick
whiptail
rsyslog

